  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.3\n- Fixed a StackOverflowException when a circular reference ran through a source collection that is\n  neither an array nor an ICollection, such as HashSet<T> or a lazily evaluated sequence.\n- Circular references that do not run through a collection are now cut instead of overflowing the\n  stack. The new `MaxCycleVisits` option (default 2) controls how often the same source and target\n  type may be visited on one branch before the cycle is cut.\n- Fixed `MaxDepth` truncation consuming the depth budget of subsequent siblings.\n- Behavior change: `MaxDepth` now counts the elements of a collection, while the collection itself\n  no longer consumes a depth level. Existing `MaxDepth` values may truncate at different points.\n- `EnableRecursionHandling` now also tracks collection elements, so an instance that occurs several\n  times within one root map call is mapped once and shared.\n- Fixed an InvalidCastException when the same source object was mapped to two different target\n  types within a single root map call.\n- `ThrowIfMaxDepthExceeded` is now also honored when the depth limit is reached on a collection\n  element, which previously produced a null element instead of an exception.\n\n2.2\n- Improved collection mapping performance.\n- Refactored internal mapping structure to favor mapping performance.\n- Fixed inconsistent source type handling between `IMapper` and `IMappingContext`.\n\n2.1\n- Added support for mapping into more collection targets, including sets and concrete collection types.\n- Improved FastCollectionFactory for thread safety and lower-allocation collection mapping.\n- Generic `Map<TSource, TTarget>()` now respects runtime types for polymorphic reference mappings.\n\n2.0\n- New mapper IMapper and mapping interfaces IMapping<TSource, TTarget>.\n- Handle circular references during mapping.\n\n1.0\n- Initial release by nabinked.",
